<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · song</p><h1 class="enc-title">Joshua Fit the Battle of Jericho</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">first half of the 19th century; published <a href="/years/1882">1882</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">&quot;Joshua Fit the Battle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jericho">Jericho</a>&quot;, also sung as &quot;Joshua Fought de Battle of Jericho&quot; or simply &quot;Joshua&quot;, is an African American spiritual. Its words tell the biblical story of the Battle of Jericho, in which Joshua led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/israelites">Israelites</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canaan">Canaan</a> (Joshua 6:15–21). Like the words of many other spirituals, they may also point to escape from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a>, in the walls that come tumbling down.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>&quot;<b>Joshua Fit the Battle of Jericho</b>&quot;, also sung as &quot;Joshua Fought de Battle of Jericho&quot; or simply &quot;Joshua&quot;, is an African American spiritual.</blockquote><a href="/songs/joshua-fit-the-battle-of-jericho">Joshua Fit the Battle of Jericho</a></li></ul></section>
